RudeConfig NEWS - User visible changes.
See ChangeLog for more detailed information on internal changes
See the end for copying conditions.

_______________________________________________________________________________
Post-release maintenance after 6.1.0

	- Reconciled the product-forward README with the 6.1.0 API and pinned all
	  install and FetchContent examples to the current stable v6.1.0 tag.
	- Added clean-consumer package smoke tests for static and shared installs,
	  the CMake package config, pkg-config, and install-prefix relocation.
	- Added packaging handoff notes for the vcpkg/Conan pilot and a release
	  checklist to keep documentation, tags, releases, and recipes aligned.

_______________________________________________________________________________
Release 6.1.0 - Matthew Flood 2026-07-30

	- CMake is now the supported build system. The earlier autotools files
	  have been retired from the current tree and remain available in v6.0.1
	  for projects that still use them. This gives current ARM and x86
	  platforms one consistent build path.
	- FetchContent consumers now receive only the library targets. Tests and
	  examples are added when rudeconfig is the top-level project.
	- The FetchContent example in README.md now pins GIT_TAG to v6.0.1
	  rather than tracking master.
	- Documentation now points to the CMake installation workflow and GitHub
	  Issues as the current support channel.

_______________________________________________________________________________
Release 6.0.1 - Matthew Flood 2026-07-30

	- Empty values are now written with their delimiter ("key = ") for
	  consistent interoperability with other ini readers.
	- deleteSection() now returns false when a section has already been
	  deleted, matching the documented contract.
	- Looking up a section that does not exist now leaves the internal
	  section map unchanged.
	- load() now reports an error when the requested path is a directory.

_______________________________________________________________________________
Release 6.0.0 - Matthew Flood 2026-07-30

	- Major version update: rude::Config is no longer copyable. This is a
	  source-level compatibility change; the shared-library ABI and soname
	  remain unchanged. Pass Config objects by reference.
	- getDataNameAt() and getDataValueAt() now return NULL for out-of-range
	  indexes, matching the documented enumeration contract.
	- Copy construction and copy assignment are now explicitly disabled to
	  reflect Config's ownership model at compile time.
	- The pkg-config prefix is now relative to ${pcfiledir}, so installations
	  made with "cmake --install --prefix <dir>" remain relocatable.
	- Config::version() now reports the library release version (for example
	  "6.0.0") and is generated from the build configuration.
	- Added regression coverage for enumeration bounds, copy semantics,
	  pkg-config relocation, and release-version reporting.

_______________________________________________________________________________
Release 5.1.0 - Matthew Flood 2026-07-30

	- Config::load() now handles end-of-file consistently on platforms where
	  char is unsigned, including Linux/ARM and Linux/PowerPC.
	- Added the CMake build system, including installed CMake package config
	  and pkg-config files; autotools remained available during this release.
	- Code updated to compile cleanly as C++17 with -Wall -Wextra, including
	  current language keywords, snprintf, and UTF-8-safe whitespace handling.
	- Added test suite (ctest) and GitHub Actions CI covering Linux
	  x86_64/ARM, macOS, and Windows, plus an ASan/UBSan job.
	- New README with verified quick-start example.

_______________________________________________________________________________
Release 5.0.5-1 - Matthew Flood 2007-02-01

	- Renamed header include guards in config.h from 
	  INCLUDED_CONFIG_H to INCLUDED_RUDE_CONFIG_H
	  The new guards are less generic and safer to use overall. 

